tracks.brief:
Implement per CONTRACTS, E2, E4, E5 and E6.

Locks:
- navigator.locks.request(DRAFT_LOCK_PREFIX+id, {ifAvailable: waitMs===0, signal}, cb). cb returns a promise that release() resolves.
- For waitMs>0, combine AbortSignal.timeout(waitMs) with opts.signal (AbortSignal.any, or a manual controller where it is missing). AbortError → null; an ifAvailable null lock → null.
- Without navigator.locks: a handle with held:false.
- lockedDraftIds: from locks.query().held names.
- withImportLock: exclusive on IMPORT_LOCK. After a 10 s wait, run anyway; the ledger and CAS keep that safe.

Pointer: sessionStorage JSON, junk-tolerant.

Mirror:
- writeMirror stores the session text unescaped: '{"v":1,…,"meta":'+JSON.stringify(meta)+',"session":'+text+'}'. Return 'too-big' above MIRROR_MAX_CHARS; QuotaExceeded → 'failed'.
- readMirrors parses entries and returns text = JSON.stringify(parsed.session).
- reconcileMirrors, per entry:
  - unparseable → quarantine (source 'mirror', the raw value) and remove;
  - locked elsewhere → skip;
  - no IndexedDB record → create;
  - IndexedDB writeSeq = baseSeq → CAS write;
  - IndexedDB writeSeq ≥ the entry's writeSeq → drop;
  - otherwise → a new draft, origin 'recovered' (never overwrite).
  Remove the mirror after an apply or drop; keep it on error.

Legacy import:
- Run under withImportLock. Never write, rewrite or delete a legacy key.
- L ('musicAtlas:daw:autosave'):
  - hash = legacyDataHash (the raw text's hash when it can't be parsed); skip when the hash is in meta 'import:ledger' {hashes, at most 200, FIFO};
  - parsed, version 1 or 2, data present → a draft. Origin 'migrated' when no ledger entry exists yet, 'recovered' after that. schema > SESSION_SCHEMA_VERSION (import it from 1.3's module) → a read-only draft with its schema recorded;
  - otherwise → quarantine 'legacy-autosave'.
- Kept slots musicAtlas:daw:kept:<ns>:<iso>: import only this user's and 'anon' ('anon' goes to '~device'). Origin 'kept', keptAt from the slot, deduped through the ledger by the hash of session.data. A malformed slot goes to quarantine 'legacy-kept'.
- musicAtlas:daw:unreadable:* (1.1's device-wide entries go to '~device'; 1.3's namespaced entries to their user) and 1.3's backup key: quarantine, deduped.
- Ownership of L:
  - the booting user when no OTHER user's namespace exists on the device: localStorage prefixes musicAtlas:daw:prefs:, musicAtlas:daw:kept:, musicAtlas:daw:mirror:, music-atlas-tutorial-progress:, oracle-synth-presets:, plus IndexedDB draft userKeys;
  - otherwise '~device'.
- Imported meta:
  - name: data.projectName or 'Untitled Project';
  - trackCount and chars;
  - schema: parsed.schema or 2;
  - projectId: data.projectId;
  - hasContent: tracks, chordRegions, markers or any notation present (true when unsure);
  - docFingerprint null;
  - baseline {source 'import', reopenable false, fingerprint null};
  - media [], mediaMissing = audio clips with a null assetId;
  - createdAt: data.timestamp, else now.
- Write the draft BEFORE the ledger entry (the worst case is a duplicate).
- claimDeviceDraft: userKey becomes the user's, claimedFrom '~device'.

Tests:
- a fake LockManager: free, held and missing; boot wait vs ifAvailable;
- the pointer per userKey;
- mirror: write, size and quota failures, every reconcile branch;
- legacy, using the real fixtures read-only (src/daw/persistence/__tests__/fixtures/v2 and v2-1.2): first import; same hash skipped; an old-tab rewrite becomes 'recovered'; kept slots with keptAt; anon → '~device'; ownership single-user vs another namespace present; unreadable and backup → quarantine deduped; future schema → read-only; legacy keys byte-identical after; two parallel imports import once.

Browser check on :5263, fresh context:
1. Seed localStorage with a v2 fixture under the legacy key and a kept slot for dev-bypass-user.
2. Dynamic-import legacyImport and draftStore and run the import twice: one draft, keys unchanged.
3. Two pages in one context: the second's acquireDraftLock(same id, {waitMs:0}) is null.

Implement pendingMedia per CONTRACTS and E8. Un-uploaded audio lives only in memory today (src/daw/audio/AudioBufferStore.ts), so R1, R7 and R5-cold lose bufferLoaded.

Capture:
- startPendingMediaCapture subscribes to subscribeAudioBufferChanges and useStore's tracks, and schedules a scan (debounced 200 ms, run in requestIdleCallback with a 1 s timeout when available).
- Pending items:
  - audio clips with no assetId (key = clip id);
  - samplerSample with no assetId and no sourceUrl (key = samplerBufferKey(sampleId)).
- Bytes for an unmapped item, in order:
  1. getOriginalAudio(key);
  2. a WeakMap<AudioBuffer, mediaId> hit;
  3. another key with the identical AudioBuffer that has an original;
  4. otherwise encode the buffer once with encode-opus (when isOpusEncodingSupported) or encode-wav. Read-only imports from src/lib/studio-assets; do not edit upload-pending.ts.
- mediaId = SHA-256 hex (crypto.subtle).
- Budget: per user 256 MiB, counted from store.usage at start plus this page's puts; navigator.storage.estimate() usage+size ≤ 0.9 of quota; device media ≤ min(1 GiB, 0.2 × quota). Over budget → missing, lastError 'quota'.
- putMedia(key `${userKey}:${mediaId}`, Blob, contentType, size, duration, rate, channels). Map key → mediaId and buffer → mediaId.
- Update useDraftStatusStore media status. pendingInMemory counts items unstored and not writing for more than 1 s; missing counts failures.

Manifest and settling:
- pendingMediaManifest() groups the CURRENT pending items that have stored media by mediaId (clipIds, samplerSampleIds). missing = pending items without stored media.
- whenMediaWritesSettled waits for in-flight puts.

Restore:
- restoreDraftMedia: for each ref, skip keys that already have a buffer.
- getMedia, then blob.arrayBuffer, then decode ONCE with getDecodeContext().decodeAudioData(bytes.slice(0)).
- Before each set, check the generation is unchanged. setAudioBuffer(key, theSameBuffer) and setOriginalAudio(key, bytes, contentType) for every clip and sampler key of that ref.
- Re-register the maps, so restored items count as stored and are not put again.
- draftMediaRestoring() is true while restores run.
- Export getDecodeContext from load-audio.ts unchanged otherwise.

Tests (fake-indexeddb, a mocked AudioContext and mocked encoders):
- a take with an original;
- split halves (shareClipAudio) map to one mediaId;
- a pasted clip with only a buffer resolves through the WeakMap;
- a buffer with no original anywhere is encoded once;
- a pending sampler sample is captured; bundled and asset-backed items are skipped;
- over budget and a quota error → missing and lastError;
- the manifest lists stored media only;
- restore shares one AudioBuffer across clips and restores originals;
- a stale generation is ignored.

Browser check on :5263:
1. Use kitchenSink's Vocals recipe (scripts/studio-perf/fixtures/kitchenSink.mjs ~296-326): add an audio clip with setAudioBuffer and setOriginalAudio.
2. Dynamic-import pendingMedia and draftStore and start the capture with userKey 'dev-bypass-user'.
3. One media record appears. Duplicating the clip adds no second record.

Implement per CONTRACTS, E3, E5, E7 and E17. Do NOT delete src/daw/hooks/useAutosave.ts or its test: editor-wiring swaps DawApp and deletes them. COPY 1.3's registry trigger subscription out of useAutosave.ts into autosave.ts: attachDocumentObserver once; the synth-store subscription calling noteSynthPatchChange.

Controller (module scope, idempotent, HMR-safe):
- start: the triggers; startPendingMediaCapture({store: getDraftStore, userKey: active userKey}); listeners for visibilitychange→hidden, pagehide and document freeze (hideFlush); a subscription to useCloudSaveStore.lastSaved that patches the active meta's cloud when lastSaved.projectId equals the store projectId and its generation is current; registerBeforeSignOut(signOutCleanup) once.
- schedule: pendingSeq++. Debounce 1000 ms, maxWait 5000 ms. Remember the generation. View-only triggers only mark viewDirty.
- write(durability, snapshot?):
  - skip while paused or with no active draft; drop when the generation moved;
  - snapshot = snapshotLiveSession(): serializeSession → JSON text, plus hashFingerprint(documentFingerprint()), hasContent = fingerprint ≠ emptyDocFingerprint() (the empty project's, computed once per page from initialProjectState over the current state), name, trackCount, schema, projectId, roomId;
  - skip when the text equals the last committed text;
  - meta takes the stored baseline and origin, cloud from lastSaved, media and mediaMissing from pendingMediaManifest();
  - store.write with expectedSeq = the committed writeSeq;
  - success: committed seq and text, status committedSeq = pendingSeq at the snapshot, remove the mirror;
  - 'conflict': fork — a new id with the current memory, origin 'fork', forkedFrom; activate it; toast 'This project was changed in another tab — your changes here were saved as a copy';
  - 'quota': prune(quota), then retry once, then status error 'quota' and ONE toast per episode, 'Storage on this device is full, so your latest changes aren't saved here.', action Manage → getSessionDeps()?.openProjectsDialog({sortBy:'size'});
  - 'unavailable': status error and one toast.
- hideFlush: synchronous. If memory is ahead (pendingSeq>committedSeq, or viewDirty): one snapshot; writeMirror {baseSeq, writeSeq: baseSeq+1}; then a strict write of that same snapshot.
- useDraftAutosave(): start on mount; on unmount, flush strict and stop.
- Mark ma:draft:write:start and ma:draft:write:end in DEV.
- After the first committed write of a draft with work, call navigator.storage.persist() once per device, on Chromium only (never Firefox). Record the result in meta 'persist'.
- status.retry = retry now (prune first when the error was quota).

Port (getDraftSessionPort), every method per the CONTRACTS comments:
- prepareUser: memoized per page and userKey. Sets meta user:<key> lastSeenAt; importLegacySessions; reconcileMirrors(locked = lockedDraftIds()); prune boot (protect locked ∪ pointer). Notices: device-found, recovered, quarantined, storage-unavailable.
- chooseResume: the pointer when its userKey matches and the draft exists and isn't read-only; otherwise the newest non-read-only draft.
- claim: an existing draft → acquireDraftLock(waitMs boot?1500:0); null → fork plan (new uuid plus its own lock). No id → a new uuid, ifAvailable.
- read: wrong user (not mine, not '~device') → 'not-found'; read-only → 'readonly'; a missing body, a JSON.parse failure or !isLoadableSession → quarantine raw, remove, 'corrupt'.
- flushOutgoing: pause; whenMediaWritesSettled(3000); write strict. Swallow a failure when the would-be meta has no work.
- retireOutgoing: 'discard', or no work → remove the draft and its mirror; otherwise patch origin 'kept' and keptAt. Release the lock; clear active; run prune switch in the background.
- activate: writeActiveDraft; status reset with paused true.
- apply: deserializeSession(parse) (1.3 bumps the generation and baselines); false or a throw → quarantine and 'corrupt'. Then meta.projectId wins over the body's. A fork gets setProjectName(name+' (copy)') and setProjectId(null).
- begin:
  - new → create {origin 'session', baseline};
  - fork → create {origin 'fork', forkedFrom, the source's baseline (its fingerprint replaced by the current hash when the source was pristine), no cloud or projectId};
  - existing → adopt: origin back to 'session'; a '~device' draft is claimed; committed seq and text come from the body.
  Then resume writes. Return null on failure (status error).
- unkeep, patchCloud, listDrafts (re-runs the legacy import; mine; device = '~device' drafts younger than 30 days; quarantine; locked), deleteDraft (refuses the active and locked drafts; removes the mirror; gcMedia), claimDeviceDraft.

signOutCleanup:
- flush when running;
- remove this user's mirrors whose IndexedDB writeSeq ≥ the mirror's;
- prune 'sign-out' (cloud-equal drafts);
- unsaved drafts stay.

devHandle: window.__MA_DRAFTS__ = { status() (DraftStatus plus activeDraftId), list(userKey?), readBody(id), flush(), mediaRestoring(), constants {DEBOUNCE_MS, MAX_WAIT_MS, MIRROR_PREFIX, ACTIVE_DRAFT_KEY} }.

Tests (fake-indexeddb plus the real useStore):
- Port ALL 11 cases of src/daw/hooks/__tests__/autosaveStarvation.test.ts to the controller (read it first): position and playback alone never schedule; a doc edit during playback is written within maxWait; a synth patch schedules; every patch field; unmount, pagehide and hidden flush; view-only rides the next write or flush.
- Controller: no writes while paused; a generation change drops a scheduled write; identical text is skipped; hidden writes the mirror and an IndexedDB write with the same writeSeq; quota → prune → retry → error and one toast; conflict → fork; persist once; lastSaved → meta.cloud.
- Port, the keptSessions invariants as a table:
  - a pristine template → removed;
  - an edited one → kept;
  - jam and collab (reopenable false) → kept;
  - discard → removed;
  - cloud-equal → removed;
  - savedComplete false → kept;
  - a restored kept draft stays the only copy;
  - '~device' claimed on begin; fork naming; adopt.
- read errors.
- persistenceMatrix: a third column, restoreDraft: begin and flush, then vi.resetModules with fake-indexeddb/auto, then claim, read and apply. Every local row equals refresh. New rows: the bytes of an un-uploaded take and of a dropped sampler sample, both in the media store and the manifest. Fix the 'Not probed' header.

Browser check on :5263 (the old boot still runs):
1. Dynamic-import the port and the autosave.
2. claim, activate and begin over the live store; add a track; within 6 s the status shows the write committed and readBody holds the track.
3. CDP Page.setWebLifecycleState frozen: the mirror key appears.
4. Report what editor-wiring must verify end to end.

Implement per CONTRACTS, E12 and spec section 6, on top of 1.3's api.ts: extend its serialization, don't duplicate it.

Verified bugs to close:
- A save still in flight while another project opens writes into the new session: api.ts:247-248 and 319-324 (probe: <scratchpad>/1.4/map/probe-save-race.mjs).
- After a deletion elsewhere, every later save 404s.
