studioApiError.ts and api.ts:
- request() throws StudioApiError: status, code from the JSON error, method, path; today's message kept for logs. A fetch TypeError → status 0.
- get and list accept {signal}.
- classifyStudioFailure: 0 → offline; 401 → signed-out; 403 → no-access; 404 → not-found; 409 → conflict; 413 → too-large; 5xx → server; AbortError from a timeout → timeout.

saveCurrentProjectToCloud(token, {fence, nameOverride, mode}), as in spec section 6:
- check the fence after EVERY await;
- a POST that resolves after the generation moved routes {projectId, cloud} to getSessionDeps()?.drafts.patchCloud(fence.draftId) and returns superseded;
- skip the PUT when the POST carried the snapshot and nothing was uploaded;
- retry a 5xx PUT once; never retry a POST automatically;
- 404 in save mode → re-create (POST under the name); projectId is set only on success;
- saveAs and asNew POST a new project WITHOUT touching store.projectId until success;
- call markDocumentBaseline({savedComplete: complete}) only if documentFingerprint is unchanged since the snapshot;
- the echo check sets complete=false on a mismatch;
- _markSessionSaved only in the same generation; the event detail is {projectId, generation}.
Keep the old saveCurrentProjectToCloud(token, nameOverride?) as a deprecated wrapper; FileMenu and LeaveSavePrompt use it until editor-wiring. ensureProjectId keeps its roomAtMint logic, fenced.

upload-pending.ts:
- uploadRecordedClip and uploadSamplerSample return early when store.projectId is null: no ensureProjectId, the draft keeps the bytes;
- they capture the generation and stamp only if it is unchanged;
- uploadPendingAudioClips accepts {fence} for its stamps;
- update splitDuringUpload.test.ts to set a projectId.

saveProject:
- returns {failed, superseded} without a toast when isOpening();
- blurs document.activeElement inside .daw-root when it is an input, textarea or contenteditable, then waits a macrotask;
- single flight: a plain save while one runs sets again=true and shares the follow-up's promise; saveAs and asNew queue separately;
- token from registerSaveAuth; none → signed-out;
- cloudSaveStore: inFlight, phase, source, error;
- on success in the same generation: setLastSaved(snapshot hash, version, complete, server updatedAt), savedCount++;
- offline: retry once on the window 'online' event.

lastSaved.ts:
- cloudOpenedRecord: fingerprint now, complete = !projectHoldsDocumentOnlyData();
- lastSavedFromDraft;
- projectHoldsDocumentOnlyData: re-export 1.3's predicate, or implement it from the registry (DOC keys with cloud 'document' differing from fieldDefault, plus track and clip fields with cloud 'document');
- documentOnlyGroups: plain names.

Toasts (src/components/utils/toast.ts): 'Project saved', or 'Project saved — <groups> stay on this device for now'; 'Saved as “X”'; 'The saved copy was deleted, so this was saved as a new project'; audio left out as today; failures in plain words (spec E12, no ids or codes).

Other files:
- useKeyboardShortcuts: Cmd/Ctrl-S calls saveProject({source:'shortcut'}), still allowed in text fields, with the e.repeat guard. Every shortcut returns early while isOpening(); Cmd-S still preventDefaults. Update the test.
- SendToSetList: ignore saved events whose projectId differs from the store's or whose generation isn't current.

Tests:
