Implement openSession per CONTRACTS, E9, E10, E11 and spec section 4: phases, per-intent list, surfaces, labels. openSession reaches drafts, collab, auth and navigation ONLY through getSessionDeps(), so its tests use fakes (fakes.ts: a fake DraftSessionPort and CollabPort).

parseBootIntent and validation:
- parseBootIntent replaces localSession.ts:628-720 with today's parameter rules, plus draft, transpose (integer, clamped to −11..11) and projects=1.
- Precedence: seeded, draft, project, template, demo, tutorial, song, practiceGenre, practiceMode, collab, jam, new, resume. consumedKeys per the spec.
- validateIntent keeps today's bootIntentError messages (localSession.ts:742-772), adds 'That draft couldn't be found.', and accepts a collab jamImport only when a jam is pending.
- editorBootCatalog: lazy lookups (getProjectTemplate, getDemoProject, getTutorial, isDiatonicMode/isScaleLesson, readPendingJam).

The machine (openSession.ts):
- One current open. A newer one aborts an older one in waiting, validating or preparing, queues behind keeping through baselining, and leaves the room during a collab load.
- Phases:
  - waiting: deps.user() non-null; then token or lessonAccess per intent; listens to onSessionDepsChanged; times out at 15 s → panel;
  - validating: validateIntent; the Premium gate → outcome upgrade (upgradeLessonId); refused 'in-room' when roomId is set and connectionStatus isn't 'disconnected', unless the source is leave-collab or the intent is resume/rejoin; a link for the room the tab is in → resume;
  - preparing: the intents.ts preparers with an AbortSignal and a 20 s fetch timeout; the E11 rule for project;
  - keeping:
    1. when isRecording or isCountingIn: store.stop(), waitingFor 'take', whenTakesSettled(10000), refused 'busy' if not settled;
    2. waitingFor 'save', whenSavesSettled(10000);
    3. flushOutgoing; DraftStorageError → refused 'storage' with today's KEEP_REFUSED text;
    4. retireOutgoing(keep);
  - switching: leaveRoom when roomId is set (BEFORE resetProjectState), resetProjectState('open:'+kind), resetUndoHistory, resetCloudSaveForSession, drafts.activate;
  - loading: apply; for a collab joiner, wait as in spec section 4 (25 s);
  - baselining: markDocumentBaseline(savedComplete per intent), resetUndoHistory, setLastSaved (cloudOpenedRecord or lastSavedFromDraft), generation, drafts.begin({source, ref, reopenable, fingerprint: hashFingerprint(documentFingerprint())}) — for draft and resume the stored baseline is kept;
  - ready: strip consumedKeys with deps.navigate(rest, {replace:true}); toasts; extras guarded by generation (offerChordAnalysis, clearJamSession, takePracticeTrack, inviteRequested, restoreMedia).
- Failure after the switch: leave the room; reset; unkeep the kept draft, then claim, read and apply it again (restored 'kept'), or begin an empty draft; set the panel.
- A cold page (sessionStore.draftId null) whose link is refused, upgraded or cancelled continues with {kind:'resume'}. A transient failure on a cold page resumes first, then shows the panel.
- sessionStore: phase, label, waitingFor, startedAt; overlay 'dim' at once on the first cold boot; 'full' after 250 ms while busy; cancellable after 3 s before keeping; 'none' at ready.
- Rejoin: only when the live draft's roomId (sessionStore.roomId) matches; otherwise clear the stale identity (collab.leaveRoom).

sessionNotices:
- kept toast: showNotice('Your previous work was kept', description name, Restore → openSession draft (source 'toast'; when deps are gone, window.location.assign('/studio/editor?draft=<id>')), secondary View → openProjectsDialog). No Restore when the new session is a room.
- fork toast; BootNotices; once per tab, unsaved-elsewhere (drafts with work, unlocked, not opened, after a link on a cold page; sessionStorage musicAtlas:daw:noticedDrafts).
- Read the legacy sessionStorage musicAtlas:daw:keptNotice once (old tabs), remove it, and show View.

useSessionBoot:
- uses useLocation and useNavigate; runs a tick after mount and on every location.key;
- a module Set of consumed keys (StrictMode);
- the first run → link or resume; later runs only when boot keys or projects=1 are present.

toast.ts: add secondaryAction (sonner cancel) with a neutral style.

Takes: useMidiRecording calls beginTake('midi') on record start and settles on commit, discard or cleanup. usePlaybackEngine calls beginTake('audio') around finishAudioTake's stopRecording promise, settling after addAudioClip or on rejection. Nothing else changes.

Tests:
- the parse table, including MSP keys and utm_* kept and legacy seeded;
- nothing changes before keeping: store snapshot, URL, drafts and collab keys all untouched on refused;
- every intent's prepare and apply against fakes;
- supersede, cancel, the 15 s timeout;
- collab ordering with a spy: leaveRoom before reset; zero Y.Doc writes, asserted through a stub bridge;
- failure after the switch restores the kept draft;
- cold refused → resume;
- E11 (unchanged / moved / offline);
- in-room refusal; stale identity cleared; rejoin guard;
- one open per key under StrictMode;
- recording waits and refusal; save settling;
- generation-guarded extras;
- toasts.
No browser checks here: the hook is mounted by editor-wiring.

Build the minimal UI in its final home per CONTRACTS, E13 and spec section 6. Stage B moves these components into the new top bar.

Model and hook:
- deriveSaveChip: pure, with the precedence and copy in spec section 6.
- useSaveChipState subscribes with selectors to useCloudSaveStore (phase, error, lastSaved), useDraftStatusStore (draftId, pendingSeq, committedSeq, error, media), useSaveStatusStore (documentVersion) and the store's projectId.
- The fingerprint compare runs throttled: at most once, ≥500 ms after the last documentVersion bump, only when lastSaved exists and versions differ.
- Components re-render only when the derived view changes. Never pass these through TransportBar or DawAppInner props: Stage A exit allows 0 top-bar commits/s outside input.

SaveStatusChip:
- fixed 150 px; Glacial 12 px regular; a 14 px icon; neutral white/10 surface; amber icon for error and audio-pending; no teal or brand yellow;
- data-testid save-chip, data-state, data-reason;
- tooltip;
- a visually hidden aria-live polite region that announces only Saved, Couldn't save and Audio not saved yet;
- in error, 'Couldn't save –' text plus a real Retry button (aria-label 'Retry save'): cloud → saveProject({source:'chip'}); device → useDraftStatusStore.getState().retry?.();
